<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill drops to 9.45 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill drops to 9.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Wednesday it raised the cut-off price at its fortnightly auction of 364-day treasury bills to 91.39 rupees from 90.83.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield dropped to 9.45 percent from 10.12.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 101 bids for 25.70 billion rupees of which it accepted 63 for 20.08 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted-average price worked out to 91.69 rupees, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
